    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0224" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/126a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The J. G. White Engineering Corporation of New York, the contractor designated by
                    the American National Red Cross, will share equally with Red Cross in making
                    advance of $100,000 on following conditions: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Chinese Government will repay contractor’s part of advance on or
                            before February 1, 1915.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Chinese Government approves contractor mentioned and will let contract
                            to it on 10% basis; Chinese Government, however, to have right to
                            subscribe for 30% of $100,000 capital stock of construction company
                            which contractor will organize, thus virtually reducing contractor’s
                            compensation to 7%.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Chinese Government and contractor both to be released from second
                            condition if contractor, with good offices of Red Cross, can not float
                            $20,000,000 loan on or before January 30, 1915, or if detailed
                            construction contract has not been signed.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Endeavor on behalf of Red Cross to obtain acceptance of these conditions by note
                    to yourself or by letter of Shah to Red Cross. Immediate action of utmost
                    importance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
